Pharmacy Inventory Categorization Prompt
Objective: Please categorize the following list of pharmaceutical items into the five specific categories provided below.

Categories:

CHRONIC MEDICINES: Medications for long-term conditions (Hypertension, Diabetes, Asthma, Cholesterol, Epilepsy, etc.).

PRESCRIPTION ONLY MEDICINES: Antibiotics, hormones, controlled substances, and high-strength medicated topicals/injections.

OTCs (Over-the-Counter): General medications for pain, minor infections, cough/cold, and common symptoms.

VITAMINS, BEAUTY AND WELLNESS: Supplements, skincare, fitness products (creatine/whey), baby care (diapers/wipes), and personal hygiene.

MEDICAL DEVICES AND SUPPLIES: Instruments, dressings, bandages, hospital equipment (drip stands/BP machines), and consumables (syringes/gloves).

Formatting Requirements:

Present the result in a Markdown Table with two columns: Item Name and Category.

Maintain the exact order in which the items appear in the source text.

If an item is listed as #N/A, include it in the table but leave the Category cell blank.

Auto-Correct: If two items are "run-on" (e.g., ProductA500mgProductB), please separate them into two distinct rows.

Cleaning: Remove stray symbols or obvious typos in the item names while maintaining the core strength/dosage information.

